{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210736,"nonce":"PSLeMpL1MDU7pUBBNmtnBAWoKPE=","title":"Subclass field slots aliased base-class fields across modules (PostPass)","message":"Fixed; see git log for the landing commit. Record migrated from session memory 2026-09-12.\n\n**STATUS: RESOLVED 2026-06-06.** Procedural-world re-enabled PostFX via `examples/game/procedural-world/postfx_setup.wren` (Tonemap + Vignette via `PostFxSetup.apply(g)`). Builds + runs without the \"Num does not implement add(_)\" or \"unknown layout id\" failures.\n\n**The fix landed in two layers:**\n1. **MIR builder** (`src/mir/builder.rs:1786-1798`) — loud panic when a subclass's superclass field layout isn't known, surfacing the error at build time instead of as silent slot aliasing.\n2. **Hatch build** (`src/hatch.rs:1129-1140 / 1301-1302 / 1409-1410`) — `build_recursive` pre-seeds the compile VM with dependency field layouts via `state.class_field_layouts` before each package compiles, then harvests the layouts back for downstream consumers.\n\n---\n\n**Historical context** (pre-fix):\n\n`@hatch:postfx` ships Tonemap / Vignette / ColorGrade / FXAA / Bloom as `PostPass` subclasses (defined in `@hatch:game/chain.wren`). When wired into the procedural-world demo via `g.postFX = PostFX.new(g); g.postFX.add(Tonemap.new(...))`, two cascading wlift codegen failures fire:\n\n1. **Initial failure: `Num does not implement 'add(_)'`** at `PostPass.onAdded_` line `_pipelines.add(pipe)`. The base-class field `_pipelines` reads back as the subclass's scalar field (e.g. Tonemap's `_exposure = 1.15`). Adding a defensive `if (!(_pipelines is List)) _pipelines = []` in `onAdded_` masks this.\n\n2. **Cascading failure: `BindGroup.create: unknown layout id`** in `buildOrCacheBindGroup_` once the defensive re-init is in place. The pipeline made it into `_pipelines`, but its bind-group layout id resolves to a value that wgpu doesn't know — same slot-routing problem one layer down.\n\n**Why:** `[[feedback-bare-var-branch-assign]]` and `[[feedback-fiber-try-stale-slot]]` are the local-variant of the same root cause; this is the class-field variant. wlift's codegen for `_name` fields in a subclass of a class declared in a different module appears to assign overlapping slots. A defensive re-init in the entrypoint method (`onAdded_`) only fixes the FIRST reference; every subsequent base-class field access from a method called on the subclass instance hits the same skew.\n\n**How to apply:** The procedural-world demo (`hatch/examples/game/procedural-world/main.wren`) keeps the `import \"@hatch:postfx\" for Tonemap, Vignette, ColorGrade` line + a commented PostFX block so re-enabling is a one-line change. The wlift fix needs to make subclass field slots NOT alias with base-class field slots — likely an `append` instead of `restart` in the class-layout pass, OR per-class slot tables with explicit base/super resolution at field-access sites.\n\nThe defensive `if (!(_pipelines is List))` guard added to `chain.wren`'s `PostPass.onAdded_` doesn't hurt and can stay — it would have flagged this faster on the user's first run.\n\nRelated sites that may carry the same bug latently:\n- `@hatch:gpu`'s `LivePipeline` (extends Pipeline)\n- Any user demo with `Game` subclasses that add private fields\n\nStatus: deferred. Tonemap shader code exists in `@hatch:gpu`'s `Shader.tonemapping`, so a direct Renderer3D-side tonemap (no PostFX, no inheritance) is a possible standalone path if needed before the wlift fix.","files":null}]}